Xcode's byacc declares %union as an anonymous union.

byacc named the union YYSTYPE from t20210328 on ("typedef union YYSTYPE
{ ... } YYSTYPE;").  The byacc Xcode ships reports 20230201 but writes
"typedef union { ... } YYSTYPE;", as byacc did before, in every header and
parser it generates from a %union.

--- a/reader.c
+++ b/reader.c
@@ -908,7 +908,7 @@
     puts_both("#define YYSTYPE_IS_DECLARED 1\n");
 
     fprintf_lineno(text_file, lineno, input_file_name);
-    puts_both("typedef union YYSTYPE");
+    puts_both("typedef union");
 
     depth = 0;
   loop:
